records.body:
Objective: make `main` the single canonical production source and complete a full architecture/codebase audit before declaring DTBK architecture-stable.

Mandatory scope:
- project and namespace dependency graph; detect cycles and reverse-layer dependencies;
- Domain purity and deterministic Engine ownership;
- Application/use-case boundaries and DI/lifetime/concurrency;
- Infrastructure/persistence/provider isolation;
- Avalonia MVVM/runtime/startup path;
- AI central-brain boundary: provider-neutral, tool/capability/policy/action/evidence flow, no direct DB/GUI/CalculationState writes;
- DataPack/SQLite/migrations/versioning/transactions;
- provenance/audit/security/error handling as explicit cross-cutting contracts;
- 15-sheet canonical projection and concrete runtime/export closure;
- duplicate/dead/legacy code and unused packages/files;
- performance and unnecessary allocations/I/O/recalculation;
- repository hygiene, while preserving all ESCON reports;
- full build/test/deep-functional/publish/runtime/Ultimate verification on the final SHA.

Non-negotiable rule: do not rewrite working deterministic business behavior merely for modernization. Every refactor must have evidence of reduced coupling, improved correctness/testability/performance, clearer ownership, or safer extensibility.

AI evolution target: future models/providers/capabilities must be additive through Application contracts/tools and Infrastructure adapters. No Domain/Engine/GUI/persistence business-contract rewrite may be required for an AI upgrade.

Completion is allowed only when every required gate is green on the same final commit SHA. Until then this issue remains open and the repository must not be described as 100% architecture-complete.
